# Committed campaign evidence is verified by sha256 over its exact bytes
# (campaign/raw_evidence.py records a digest per file; the offline verification
# test re-hashes them). Any end-of-line normalization on checkout would rewrite
# those bytes and break every recorded digest on that clone — the evidence would
# read as tampered when nothing was tampered with.
#
# `-text` disables EOL conversion entirely, so these files round-trip byte for
# byte on every platform. Do not remove this without re-hashing the evidence.
campaign/results/** -text

# The scene is a USD crate (binary). Its identity in run manifests is the graph
# fingerprint from scenes.scene_contract, not this file's hash — crate re-saves
# are not byte-reproducible — but it must still never be line-ending mangled.
*.usd binary
